Nitrous Oxide is Emitted During Composting
It appears that the composting process results in significant production and emission of nitrous
oxide. This must be taken into consideration when estimating GHG emissions during
composting. The method of composting appears to have a significant effect on N20 emission.
Nitrous oxide emission is generally higher during thermophilic composting when the air supply
is limited as observed with heaped manure (Martins & Dewes 1992). This is consistent with the
theory of increased N20 emission under a combination of aerobic/anaerobic decomposition.
